<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16798" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exemptĭo</span></b> , ōnis,
			f.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen., <i>a taking out</i>, <i>removing</i>
			(not in Cic. or Caes.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alvi (apiarii),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 3, 16, 34</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">favorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					3, 18, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cretae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					19, 5, 16</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			jurid. Lat., <i>a detention</i> of a person summoned
			before court, <i><span class="en">Dig. 2, 7, 5</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">ib.
		4</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
